    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>This brass censer is reassuringly warm to the touch.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> The censer has 10 charges and regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can cast a spell on the Censer Spells table from it (save DC 18), expending the number of charges it shows.</p><p><strong>Censer Spells</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplBanishment]{Banishment}</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplBless00000]{Bless}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.spells.Item.Ydjq7AY2mw80wgeM]{Circle of Power}</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDispelMagi]{Dispel Magic}</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplRemoveCurs]{Remove Curse}</td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Protective Incense.</strong> As a Magic action while holding the censer, you can make magical smoke billow from it, filling a 30-foot Emanation originating from the censer for 1 hour or until you end it (no action required). The area is Lightly Obscured, and creatures of your choice (including you) gain the benefits of the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbEvilAndGoodPr]{Protection from Evil and Good} spell while within it. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Spirit Imprisonment.</strong> When a creature dies within 30 feet of you while you hold the censer, you can draw its soul into the censer and trap it there.</p><p>While its soul is trapped in the censer, the creature can’t be restored to life, and any trait that would let it revive—such as a @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.actors24.Actor.mmBarbedDevil000]{Barbed Devil}’s Diabolical Restoration or a @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.actors24.Actor.mmLich0000000000]{Lich}’s Spirit Jar—doesn’t work. The censer holds only one soul at a time. A soul stays trapped for 100 years, until you take a Magic action to release it, or until the censer is destroyed.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The censer has the following random properties (see the <em>Dungeon Master’s Guide</em>):</p><ul><li><p>1 minor beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying the Censer.</strong> If it doesn’t hold a soul, the censer is destroyed after being submerged in the River Styx for 1 year.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-Uwi2rYE4rYromCvp\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ. <em>Circle of Power</em> vient du compendium Spells.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
